  "framing_differences_vs_real_server": [
    "Init frames (`|init|battle`, `|title|`, `|j|`) copy what a live local server sent (p1: init+own join, then p2's `|j|`; p2: both joins); real timing relative to the first sim update chunk is not reproduced, only the order.",
    "Each sim `update` is delivered as one frame per player containing that player's channel (|split| extraction identical to sim/battle.ts); the real server sends room.update() broadcast buffers, which may batch several sim updates or `|inactive|` timer lines; no timer lines are produced offline.",
    "`sideupdate |request|` is delivered as its own frame AFTER the update frame with an incrementing room-wide `rqid` appended as the last JSON key (room-battle.ts receive).",
    "Both players receive every frame of a sim output batch before either player's reply is submitted (p1 then p2); in production the arrival order of the two replies is racy.",
    "RoomBattlePlayer.request.isWait bookkeeping is mirrored: 'There's nothing to choose' and 'too late' errors are produced; the `|rqid` suffix check and the battle timer are not (our players never send an rqid suffix).",
    "No `|:|` scrollback timestamp, no `|inactive|` lines, no `|uhtml|` open-team-sheet prompts, no `|deinit|`/`|l|` or lobby `|pm|`/`|updatesearch|` frames. Frame kinds/order/request key order were checked against a live capture (reports/w5_cf0_1_frame_parity.json)."
  ],
